Sentry Error Tracking Integration Complete ✅
I've integrated Sentry error tracking into your Next.js project. Here's what was added:

Configuration Files (root):

sentry.client.config.ts - Browser-side error tracking with session replay
sentry.server.config.ts - Server-side error tracking
sentry.edge.config.ts - Edge runtime (proxy) error tracking
instrumentation.ts - Next.js instrumentation hook
Updated next.config.ts - Wrapped with Sentry webpack plugin
Error Handling Components:

src/app/error.tsx - App-level error page
src/app/global-error.tsx - Root layout error page
src/components/providers/ErrorBoundary.tsx - React error boundary with HOC
Utilities:

src/lib/error-tracking.ts - Centralized error tracking API
src/lib/error-tracking.example.ts - Usage examples (delete after reviewing)
Other Changes:

Merged rate limiting from middleware.ts into proxy.ts (deleted middleware.ts due to Next.js 16 conflict)
Updated .env.example with Sentry environment variables
To activate Sentry:

Create a project at sentry.io
Add to your .env:
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://your-key@your-org.ingest.sentry.io/your-project-id
SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=your-auth-token  # Optional, for source maps
SENTRY_ORG=your-org-slug
SENTRY_PROJECT=your-project-slug
The build errors you see are pre-existing issues with static generation and cookies, not related to Sentry.